      "notes": "Montages, captions and native complete diagrams reviewed. Native18 confirms the complete eight-piece final source board after e7: White Kh1/e7 against Kd3/Ba5/c6/d5/g6/h5, BLACK to move. Native16/17 support the preceding a5/Bxa5 diversion; the bishop is on a5, not b4 or b6 as in related clips. The new Bd8/e8=Q and Kc4/e8=Q comparisons are independently supplied legal continuations after the clip ends, not recovered source moves. No pawn is removed when promotion leaves eight pieces. Three bounded twelve-ply searches reused the original 213 exact supported probes and added 160, leaving 373 saved responses and 208 partial White policy choices. The last search visited 513 nodes before its explicit new-query cap; it did not produce a complete root certificate. All saved responses retain the actual full queried FEN and URL; the partial policy is not complete outcome evidence. Further work must check every Black reply after e7, prioritize immediate legal promotion over unnecessary engine-suggested king moves, and finish all queen-versus-bishop-and-four-pawn conversions or actual mates. No positive engine estimate or partial certificate is treated as proof. Earlier eight-piece e6 draft, all review history and original images/captions remain preserved; source material is available and the status remains pending analysis.",
